      "budget_share": 0.5,
      "why": "Full pipelining gives 1 result/cycle, so throughput_msps = Fmax/1000. To guarantee >=1 MSPS we need Fmax >= 1000 MHz, which is impossible on Artix-7; therefore the pipelined family is only viable if the throughput constraint is interpreted as sustained rate where latency does not block the loop, or if Fmax is high enough. However, since Artix-7 Fmax is typically 200-400 MHz, pipelined alone cannot meet >=1 MSPS unless we accept that 'throughput' here means the loop can sample at 1 MSPS with N+2 latency (which is fine for a control loop). The area is dominated by N stages of registers. Minimizing N and data_width minimizes area. We search low N (10-16) to balance accuracy (need <=2^-10 error) and area. data_width 12-16 ensures output precision. angle_guard and frac_guard kept low to save area."
    },
    {
      "family": "pipelined_m",
      "ranges": [
        {
          "param": "data_width",
          "low": 12,
          "high": 16
        ,
          "choices": null
        },
        {
